.TH DIG 1 "2026-05-22" "hako" "hako utilities"
.SH NAME
dig \- look up DNS A records for a domain
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dig
.RI [@ nameserver ]
.I domain
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dig
queries the DNS for A (IPv4 address) records of
.I domain
and prints each address on its own line.
.PP
By default the nameserver
.B 8.8.8.8
(Google Public DNS) is used.
An alternate nameserver can be specified by prepending
.BI @ address
(an IPv4 address) to the argument list.
.PP
If no A records are found a message of the form
.I domain\fB: no A records found\fR
is printed and the command exits 0.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "dig example.com"
Look up A records using the default nameserver.
.TP
.B "dig @1.1.1.1 example.com"
Look up A records using Cloudflare's resolver.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (records found or not found).
.TP
.B 1
Wrong number of arguments, or a DNS error occurred.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dig (1),
.BR host (1),
.BR hako (1)
